"svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 320 320\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"plan\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"320\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#14171c\"/>\n<rect x=\"56.6\" y=\"97.9\" width=\"206.9\" height=\"196.6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#3a4250\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M160.0,284.1 L211.3,141.5 L108.7,141.5 Z\" fill=\"#ffffff10\" stroke=\"#ffffff30\"/>\n<rect x=\"149.0\" y=\"277.1\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#e0e0e0\"/><text x=\"140.0\" y=\"306.1\" class=\"lb\">Camera</text>\n<circle cx=\"160.0\" cy=\"160.0\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#c9a27e\"/><polygon points=\"160.0,168.8 163.1,160.0 156.9,160.0\" fill=\"#c9a27e\"/>\n<text x=\"174.0\" y=\"150.0\" class=\"lb\">Subject</text>\n<line x1=\"86.9\" y1=\"236.8\" x2=\"107.0\" y2=\"216.6\" stroke=\"#f5c542\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" opacity=\"0.8\"/>\n<circle cx=\"86.9\" cy=\"236.8\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#f5c542\"/>\n<text x=\"72.9\" y=\"223.8\" class=\"lb\">Spotlight with a blinds gobo</text>\n</svg>",
"look": "Hard stripes of light across the actor and the wall. Secrets, danger, a hot office afternoon.",
"html": "<p>The blinds gobo in the Spotlight SE, used as the key. The stripes carry the mood, and the dark gaps hide part of the face. It's the oldest noir trick there is.</p>",
"lights": [
{
"label": "Spotlight with a blinds gobo",
"fixture": "amaran COB 200x S",
"modifier": "amaran Spotlight SE 36 degree",
"dist_m": 2.09,
"dist_ft": 6.8,
"where": "45° camera left, 2.0 ft (0.60 m) above the eyes",
"power": 8,
"cct": 4300
}
],
"props": [],
"camera": {
"body": "Blackmagic PYXIS 6K",
"lens": "50 mm",
"exposure": "T2.8, ISO 800, 1/50, 5600 K",
"meter": "122 lux (T2.8)"
},
"steps": [
"Put the Spotlight SE on the 200x S with the blinds gobo, about 6 feet away at 45 degrees, a little above the eyes.",
"Tilt the gobo a few degrees so the stripes aren't perfectly level.",
"Move the actor until a bright stripe lands across the eyes, or across the mouth if the eyes should stay hidden.",
"Keep the rest of the room dark. Add nothing unless the shadow side needs a touch of bounce."
],
"watch": [
"Small head moves change which stripe hits the eyes. Rehearse and give the actor a mark.",
"Stripes on a moving actor flicker across the face. That can be great, or distracting."
],
"vary": [
"Push the light farther away and refocus. Stripes get finer.",
"Use a real set of blinds as a cookie in front of the 600d instead."
],
